1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,721
Wacky Wheels builds cars just in time — no parts inventory.

2
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:12,539
A late shipment, a plant outage, or a bad lot ripples into schedules, dealers, loaner cars, and owners.

3
00:00:12,539 --> 00:00:16,144
Messages arrive as messy emails and chats.

4
00:00:16,144 --> 00:00:22,552
Our Control Tower turns each one into exactly the actions the handbook demands — and proves why.

5
00:00:22,552 --> 00:00:29,907
One small local language model, Qwen two point five three B, only classifies and copies phrases.

6
00:00:29,907 --> 00:00:42,500
Everything else is deterministic code: a knowledge graph of seventeen thousand nodes, specialist agents, a verifier, and a digital twin that dry-runs every plan before the real server sees it.

7
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,986
The rule is simple: the LLM reads, code decides.

8
00:00:46,986 --> 00:00:50,184
Here is the live Event Operations desk.

9
00:00:50,184 --> 00:00:53,000
Fifteen events from the scored run.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,618
We open E-09 — a supplier delay on surround-view cameras into Huntsville.

11
00:00:58,618 --> 00:01:01,486
The model extracts the phrases.

12
00:01:01,486 --> 00:01:05,328
Code resolves them to shipment, part, and plant.

13
00:01:05,328 --> 00:01:08,276
The graph path shows who is affected.

14
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:15,263
The twin plans reschedules and transfers, ranks Platinum and Gold for loaners, and notifies dealers.

15
00:01:15,263 --> 00:01:18,500
Every action cites a rule and evidence.

16
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:26,026
E-01 is a compound digest: a San Antonio outage and a chip delay to Princeton, in one message.

17
00:01:26,026 --> 00:01:29,236
Next Friday resolves to March nineteenth.

18
00:01:29,236 --> 00:01:34,684
One shared slot ledger, one notify per dealer, loaners ranked together.

19
00:01:34,684 --> 00:01:38,197
The before-and-after heatmap shows blocked days.

20
00:01:38,197 --> 00:01:41,092
E-03 is a quality hold.

21
00:01:41,092 --> 00:01:43,434
The lot is identified.

22
00:01:43,434 --> 00:01:46,592
Unsold vehicles are stopped at dealers.

23
00:01:46,592 --> 00:01:49,131
Sold owners are contacted.

24
00:01:49,131 --> 00:01:53,105
Noise like E-05 makes zero tool calls.

25
00:01:53,105 --> 00:01:57,302
An unconfirmed rumor escalates once — nothing else.

26
00:01:57,302 --> 00:02:02,394
The verifier tab shows plan checks and twin world checks, all green.

27
00:02:02,394 --> 00:02:05,868
The Audit trail filters by rule or dealer.

28
00:02:05,868 --> 00:02:09,750
Human review can approve or reject escalations.

29
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:13,263
Managers edit policy without hard-coding.

30
00:02:13,263 --> 00:02:20,210
Policy Studio versions event types, playbooks, rules, switches, and verifier checks.

31
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:23,500
Handbook V1 stays the scored baseline.

32
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,368
Preview impact runs twin-only.

33
00:02:26,368 --> 00:02:28,921
Publish creates a new version.

34
00:02:28,921 --> 00:02:34,657
The official run still refuses edited profiles unless you pass the policy flag.

35
00:02:34,657 --> 00:02:37,065
What-if is a sandbox.

36
00:02:37,065 --> 00:02:41,381
Pick plant outage, supplier delay, or quality hold.

37
00:02:41,381 --> 00:02:46,026
Fill plant, part, supplier, and dates from the tables.

38
00:02:46,026 --> 00:02:51,802
The normal planner and verifier run on the twin only — nothing is sent to any server.

39
00:02:51,802 --> 00:03:03,750
You see affected orders, units delayed, Platinum and Gold customers, dealers to notify, loaners needed versus available, transfers, promise misses, and the graph path.

40
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,894
Compare two scenarios side by side.

41
00:03:06,894 --> 00:03:10,855
Everything is labeled simulation, not executed.

42
00:03:10,855 --> 00:03:14,250
Operations health reads only from traces.

43
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:22,355
Per-stage timing: extract, resolve, gate, plan, verify, twin, execute, and read-back.

44
00:03:22,355 --> 00:03:29,657
Totals, slowest events, cache hit rate, failure count — which should be zero — and the model used.

45
00:03:29,657 --> 00:03:34,921
The Daily briefing is plain business language generated from the same traces.

46
00:03:34,921 --> 00:03:50,960
Events by type, incidents handled, actions by tool, customers affected, Platinum and Gold protected, loaners assigned versus requested, quality lots held, vehicles stopped, open escalations, zero failed calls, and three highlights.

47
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:54,460
Download Markdown or a one-page PDF.

48
00:03:54,460 --> 00:04:02,421
Self-check on the recorded run: fifteen of fifteen green, seven hundred sixty-six writes, zero failed calls.

49
00:04:02,421 --> 00:04:04,381
LLM reads.

50
00:04:04,381 --> 00:04:06,315
Code decides.

51
00:04:06,315 --> 00:04:09,894
Every action cites a rule and a graph path.

52
00:04:09,894 --> 00:04:14,460
That is the Wacky Wheels Control Tower — ready for Hack the Highway.
